==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|hole in the wall}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[hole]]-in-the-[[wall]]|s|holes-in-the-wall}}

# A [[restaurant]], [[shop]] or other [[establishment]] [[cater]]ing to [[customer]]s that is particularly [[inconspicuous]] and easily [[overlooked]].
# {{lb|en|colloquial|chiefly|British}} An [[automated teller machine]] (ATM).

====Usage notes====
Although either plural can be used for both meanings, ''[[hole-in-the-walls]]'' tends to be most commonly used for the "obscure place" sense, and ''[[holes-in-the-wall]]'' is more frequently used to mean "automated teller machines".

Used to refer to an inconspicuous establishment, the term has a connotation that the quality of the food or rendered services deserves recognition.

The British sense of an automated teller machine may have originated as a trademark of [[w:Barclays|Barclays]].

